cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "pi-fixed-supply — Pi's ledger headers report 100,000,000,000 π, and the chain shows no issuance"
abstract: >-
  A read-only, zero-dependency measurement: every ledger header examined on Pi Mainnet reports
  `totalCoins` = 100,000,000,000 π, and the chain shows no issuance operation and no increment of the
  issuance counter — consistent with the documented protocol rule that removed native issuance before
  Pi's genesis. The claim is verified by decoding the raw header bytes (including the issuance counter,
  which the public API does not expose), by binding those bytes to the network locally with SHA-256
  (sha256(header) = the ledger hash, and adjacent headers chained), by sweeping the observable ledger
  range for the documented cap, and by cross-checking the API's JSON summary against the header it
  summarises. It proves nothing about circulating supply, allocation, unlock schedules, price, or any
  future protocol change.
